# Question: when a config user takes the same username as the stored ZeFS
# recovery user and references a login-service set allowing only rest, is that
# shadowing config user gated as an ordinary account (refused on SSH and Web,
# admitted on REST) while the shadowed stored password stops working everywhere?
# Why a unit test cannot decide it: only seeding a real ZeFS store and running
# mergeAuthUsers in a live daemon proves the recovery exemption follows the
# credential source (ReservedRecoveryProfile), never the username string.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-14 (OD-2 option a) -- config user shadowing recovery username is gated normally
# PREVENTS: granting login-service exemption by username instead of ReservedRecoveryProfile

option=timeout:value=60s
option=storage:value=disk
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/login-service-shadowed-recovery-name $PORT $PORT2 $PORT3:timeout=50s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: shadowing config user gated as ordinary account on SSH/Web and admitted on REST
reject=stderr:contains=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
